WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.890
Here's some working that
looks perfectly reasonable.

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:08.910
Differentiate each bit, then multiply:
two x times three x squared gives six x

3
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:09.930
cubed.

4
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.750
Plot the curve and draw its
tangent at x equals two.

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:19.280
So is the derivative of x squared times
x cubed really just two x times three

6
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.600
x squared?

7
00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.470
In this mission, you'll
use standard derivatives:

8
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.610
x to the n differentiates
to n x to the n minus one.

9
00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.330
And you'll meet the product rule, for
differentiating a product of two functions.

10
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:37.450
Your mission: decide whether the derivative
of x squared times x cubed is just

11
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.630
two x times three x squared.
